# Pairs with MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites, and reproduces production's move fence
# as it stood before issue #4525 was fixed (#4557): the fence lives only in the source
# activation's memory, so an activation that crashes after the copy comes back
# unfenced, takes and acknowledges a write on the source, and the flip - which
# re-checks nothing about the source - switches the stream to a copy without it.
# The base keeps a durable fence that every new activation re-derives, and the
# flip requires it still held.
MODULE: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWritesFenceInMemoryOnly
TARGET: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the fence is in-memory only and the flip is unguarded, so a re-activated source acknowledges a write the flip discards
PERTURBS: ShardCrash, MoveSwitch

--- FIND
    /\ afence' = (dfence # NoMove /\ ~lapsed)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the new activation does not know about any fence.
    /\ afence' = FALSE
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ move[m] = "copied"
    /\ dfence = m
    /\ durable' = {o \in moveCopy[m] : o >= tail}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the flip's compare-and-swap checks only the placement version.
    /\ move[m] = "copied"
    /\ durable' = {o \in moveCopy[m] : o >= tail}
--- END
